{"w":2400,"h":2857,"lines":[{"t":"Test 4","w":0.053730805714925139,"h":0.013366138626429658,"x":0.079535981139248785,"c":1,"y":0.065264605082376415},{"y":0.10913939776971149,"w":0.69222966512044271,"c":1,"h":0.022841219304740812,"t":"Having already tested 1,000 children, the researchers will now embark on retesting them.","x":0.079483700265199242},{"t":"They intend to look not only at test results, but also at variables such as the standard of","h":0.020762651095113327,"x":0.079495646115641611,"y":0.12768737081516512,"w":0.68357915242513023,"c":1},{"x":0.077749771324996331,"y":0.14593539963089741,"h":0.021811712864314492,"c":1,"t":"schooling, the environment and the teaching practices themselves. It's possible that one","w":0.68013844807942703},{"t":"of the causes of low performance is the lack of pupil-centred teaching methods; in many","x":0.079529817209855913,"h":0.02057233534132874,"w":0.69041849772135411,"c":1,"y":0.16450188963763646},{"x":0.079497723106872184,"t":"Indian primary schools the teacher dominates and there is little room for independent","y":0.18291227051597014,"w":0.66973612467447907,"c":1,"h":0.02112811123932723},{"h":0.017864741171215615,"w":0.076077264149983725,"t":"learning.","x":0.077018021155469713,"c":1,"y":0.203937850157353},{"x":0.07958476331120333,"t":"Although the findings are at a preliminary stage, Tsimpli and her team have found that the","y":0.23967809661500172,"w":0.70415227254231771,"h":0.017589345522240563,"c":1},{"x":0.079527609751128991,"h":0.02100839274508548,"c":1,"y":0.25655417466845409,"t":"medium of instruction used in schools, especially English, may hold back those children who","w":0.72503092447916662},{"x":0.079522911059160317,"c":1,"y":0.27527460812664328,"t":"have little familiarity with, or exposure to, the language before starting school and outside","h":0.02048135654671035,"w":0.70255182902018232},{"y":0.2933947269204491,"t":"of school life. According to Tsimpli, most of the evidence from this and other projects shows","w":0.72500615437825522,"h":0.019771414423756406,"c":1,"x":0.079541564637686885},{"c":1,"w":0.6991813151041667,"x":0.079468075532916585,"t":"that English instruction for children from low socio-economic areas might not be the best","y":0.30896094496220672,"h":0.02284216563796726},{"c":1,"y":0.32835438557488772,"t":"way for them to learn, at least in the first three years of primary education.","w":0.58493489583333336,"h":0.02274189836249807,"x":0.079488249228567162},{"t":"'What we would recommend for everyone, not just low socio-economic status children,","x":0.079537492722665776,"y":0.36613141693754092,"h":0.020219190209123772,"w":0.67829310099283857,"c":1},{"w":0.70079452514648444,"t":"would be to start learning in the language they feel comfortable learning in... English can","h":0.019972623020222846,"c":1,"x":0.08126083912605879,"y":0.3846866116089438},{"y":0.40217802414279569,"h":0.0227305904145505,"w":0.68527440388997385,"c":1,"t":"still be used, but perhaps not as the medium of instruction in primary schools. It could,","x":0.07949294682536831},{"t":"for example, be one of the subjects that are being taught alongside other subjects. We are","w":0.69394312540690095,"y":0.42061014890437365,"x":0.079497007596642341,"h":0.021514456116961345,"c":1},{"y":0.4398096933108504,"c":1,"h":0.019686726275818467,"x":0.081255269388025561,"t":"not suggesting that English be withdrawn - that ship has sailed - but we perhaps have to","w":0.6869687906901043},{"y":0.45663774749682451,"t":"think more about learner needs. There is perhaps too much uniformity in teaching and less","x":0.079519517121887207,"w":0.70774937947591143,"h":0.021606904464305243,"c":1},{"h":0.020643806857942648,"c":1,"t":"tailoring to the children's language abilities and needs, says Tsimpli.","y":0.47515745297541856,"x":0.079584785887798826,"w":0.53287195841471358},{"w":0.71117284138997394,"t":"While the preliminary results show there is no difference in general intelligence among boys","h":0.019469991941565401,"c":1,"x":0.081271194426898313,"y":0.51297693086140472},{"h":0.017578157033846908,"w":0.68166091918945315,"x":0.079584765522536044,"c":1,"t":"and girls from slum areas versus those from urban poor backgrounds, an unanticipated","y":0.53184044788699081},{"t":"finding has been that children from slum backgrounds do not seem to lag behind children","x":0.081254387051508087,"h":0.020121450938070717,"c":1,"y":0.54931295533591118,"w":0.6973508707682291},{"w":0.71981272379557293,"h":0.019539761660063992,"t":"from other urban poor backgrounds - and in some cases outperform them (e.g. in numeracy","y":0.56805620448549432,"c":1,"x":0.081267698497446472},{"t":"and literacy tasks). According to the researchers, this unexpected finding may be down to","h":0.018926880091032494,"w":0.69550170898437491,"x":0.081314890455909297,"c":1,"y":0.58572428247967123},{"h":0.018927897165670893,"c":1,"y":0.60461861442539933,"x":0.081314886278696763,"t":"the life experiences of children growing up in slums. They are likely to mature faster and","w":0.68685119628906255},{"w":0.64545323689778644,"c":1,"x":0.081238448117489578,"y":0.62274855038026355,"t":"come into closer contact with the numeracy skills essential for day-to-day survival.","h":0.019511571207440181},{"y":0.65885629989753636,"c":1,"w":0.67311864217122397,"h":0.020053011958961142,"t":"The project has already caught the attention of government ministers, who are keen to","x":0.081264848869697343},{"y":0.67651219750025804,"t":"use the findings of the study to inform and adjust school policy in Delhi and the wider","x":0.081215635087723684,"w":0.67493067423502606,"h":0.020869534694706315,"c":1},{"t":"stateiẠỊThey are as keen as us to understand how the challenging context of deprivation","w":0.67830652872721353,"y":0.69594255075790257,"c":1,"x":0.081259098304875432,"h":0.01941909015887755},{"x":0.081260412697778575,"w":0.69386474609374993,"h":0.019048740181412338,"c":1,"t":"can be attenuated when focusing on the languages children learn and use while at school.","y":0.71461481920797487},{"t":"Our findings don't mean you're doomed if you're poor. It may be that these low learning","x":0.083044990043975989,"y":0.73401162762421834,"h":0.017562900246899771,"c":1,"w":0.68685119628906244},{"t":"outcomes are because of the way education is provided in India, with a huge focus on Hindi","y":0.74993303546624779,"w":0.72166437784830728,"x":0.081220017643021072,"h":0.023197745342534937,"c":1},{"h":0.021523734587234888,"t":"and English as the mediums of instruction, to the potential detriment of children unfamiliar","x":0.081252141211982876,"y":0.7688118794547939,"c":1,"w":0.72331344604492187},{"h":0.019067245066958449,"w":0.31141868591308597,"t":"with those languages, explains Tsimpli.","y":0.78779069751650566,"x":0.081314878704356677,"c":1},{"x":0.081284296076679821,"w":0.68692382812499997,"t":"'Language is central to the way knowledge is transferred - so the medium of instruction","y":0.82388428639772604,"h":0.01973738513516754,"c":1},{"y":0.84008744826378845,"w":0.68697535196940107,"x":0.081253430982927935,"t":"is obviously hugely influential. We hope to ... show that problem solving, numeracy and","h":0.022187257663948357,"c":1},{"t":"literacy can and do improve in children who are educated in a language of instruction they","x":0.081245047458888844,"y":0.85995511011909764,"w":0.70776117960611984,"h":0.021501581847375717,"c":1},{"w":0.72333363850911458,"h":0.020178804871416989,"y":0.87892676976876383,"t":"know. The trick may be to bridge school skills with life skills and make use of the richness of","c":1,"x":0.082977824688276289},{"c":1,"w":0.71280273437499997,"t":"a child's life experience to help them learn in the most effective ways possible,' says Tsimpli.","x":0.081314900632569145,"y":0.89534883734726012,"h":0.020348836526410174},{"c":1,"t":"86","h":0.014534882851794828,"y":0.96366279098689334,"x":0.083044983164500916,"w":0.02249134858449299}]}